[caption id="attachment_139046" align="aligncenter" width="300"]<img class="size-medium wp-image-139046" src="http://35.224.26.164/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/1-86-300x233.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="233" /> Adam Blackstone is able to keep his creative files secure with the OWC ThunderBay 4, Envoy Pro EX and Thunderbolt 2 Dock. (PRNewsfoto/OWC)[/caption]

&nbsp;

OWC®, a leading zero emissions Mac and PC technology company, is delighted to announce that Adam Blackstone, multi-instrumentalist and musical director extraordinaire, will be using OWC products during the Super Bowl LII™ Halftime Show featuring Justin Timberlake, taking place on Sunday, February 4, 2018.

Mr. Blackstone has been producing music since he played drums at his family's church as a child."I fell in love with the bass guitar, fell in love with reading music, fell in love with orchestration, fell in love with jazz," he recalled. "I met members of The Roots while in college. From there, that was all she wrote," he concluded.

&nbsp;

Mr. Blackstone's role as a musical director has many prospects,"not only playing live, not only teaching parts, not only scoring, but also a major part of what you guys hear as the audience and as the viewer is the programming aspect.  I have to take the studio recording and translate that in a live atmosphere.  That takes a lot of time, preparation, and I need my products that I work with to be stable, mobile, compatible and to work at all times. And OWC is all of that for me. It helps me stay in creative mode when what I don't have to worry about day to day is 'is this session going to load back up, am I going to lose my files, is it not going to load up, is it going to crash on me in the middle of the show?' I've had none of that, we've done everything from Coachella, Austin City Limits, we just did the Grand Prix, 80,000 out there, all working on our OWC drives."

He continued "As of late, working on the Super Bowl, the <a class="linkOnClick" href="https://www.owcdigital.com/products/envoy-pro-ex" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" data-include="300592975">Envoy Pro EX</a> has been my go-to drive during this whole creative process. I'm recording off of that drive, and taking it back to Justin, for him to approve. That's the type of functionality that I'm always looking for, and that I think is the main asset, is that stability that OWC provides for me in my work environment."

&nbsp;

When inquired about his workflow and connecting his computers, drives, and accessories, Mr. Blackstone exuded "One of the other great things about OWC is their <a class="linkOnClick" href="https://www.owcdigital.com/products/docks" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" data-include="300592975">Thunderbolt 2 Dock and Thunderbolt 3 Dock</a>, whichever you prefer. I am using it for a plethora of things, I'm able to go directly into the dock from my external hard drives without there being any long cabling, any mess on my workstation, it has USB, Thunderbolt, FireWire and for those who don't know, also Audio In/Out as well. It's a lifesaver on the road, anything you need mobility for, this can do it. Its functionality seems limitless and it helps, especially in this new age of computers we have, when there are limited ports and things like that, this is what you need to get to work at a fast pace, with multiple drives."

&nbsp;

OWC is honored to be a trusted part of the production process for the halftime show, an event that is expected to be seen by more than 110 million viewers. Mr. Blackstone beamed "OWC inspires me to be creative and to open my mind to limitless possibilities for how I create music, how I make music, how I present music to the world, and how you receive the music is a big part of what happens through that creative process, and that's why I need a product that works like it does, as hard for me as I do for the people in music."

&nbsp;

<b>About <span class="xn-person">Adam Blackstone</span>
</b><a class="linkOnClick" href="http://www.adamblackstone.com/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" data-include="300592975"><span class="xn-person">Adam Blackstone</span></a> is a multi-instrumentalist, musical director, songwriter, producer, and bassist. He is currently the musical director for Nicki Minaj and <span class="xn-person">Justin Timberlake</span>, and was the Band Leader for the soundtrack of the motion picture "The Greatest Showman". He has worked with such additional artists as <span class="xn-person">Ed Sheeran</span>, <span class="xn-person">Alicia Keyes</span>, <span class="xn-person">Pharrell Williams</span>, Rihanna, Band Perry, <span class="xn-person">Tim McGraw</span>, <span class="xn-person">Faith Hill</span>, Rascal Flatts, Maroon 5, and more. He is the Musical Director for the Super Bowl LII Halftime Show.

